r Pudding","a":"1971-05-12","l":28},{"s":8,"e":10,"t":"The Whole Fish Story","a":"1971-05-19","l":28,"img":"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/71713/4206927.jpg"},{"s":8,"e":11,"t":"VIP Veal: Poitrina Farcie","a":"1971-05-26","l":28},{"s":8,"e":12,"t":"Brochettes, Kebabs and Skewers","a":"1971-06-02","l":28},{"s":8,"e":13,"t":"Rye Bread","a":"1971-06-09","l":28},{"s":8,"e":14,"t":"Flaming Fish","a":"1971-06-16","l":28},{"s":8,"e":15,"t":"Summer Salads","a":"1971-06-23","l":28},{"s":8,"e":16,"t":"Lobster Show","a":"1971-06-30","l":28,"img":"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/71713/4206933.jpg"},{"s":8,"e":17,"t":"Coq Au Vin Alias Chicken Fricassee","a":"1971-07-07","l":28,"d":"The French Chef's Julia Child prepares Coq Au Vin Alias Chicken Fricassee. Take chicken, onions, and mushrooms, simmer them in red wine for coq au vin, or in white wine for an old fashioned fricassee. This episode offers two recipes in one–two famous dishes that will teach you a lot more about cooking than just how to stew a chicken."},{"s":8,"e":18,"t":"Mousse Au Chocolat (Chocolate Mousse)","a":"1971-07-14","l":28,"d":"Julia Child demonstrates how to make a classic French chocolate mousse. She shows techniques for whipping egg whites, melting chocolate, and molding the dish for an elegant presentation, often serving it with langues de chat (cat's tongues) cookies."},{"s":8,"e":19,"t":"Quiche Lorraine and Company","a":"1971-07-21","l":28,"d":"Sudden guests? Julia shows you how to bake them a quiche, in this episode of The French Chef. It’s fast, fancy and foolproof. Here’s the ultimate motivation for learning to make your own pie dough. Julia teaches you how to concoct an expert pie-crust dough and use it for open face, main dish pies, such as custard and bacon, spinach, and /or crab."},{"s":8,"e":20,"t":"To Suff a Sausage","a":"1971-07-28","l":28,"d":"Julia shows how to use a funnel, pastry tube, or stuffing horn to fill casings, and explains how to twist and tie them into links, emphasizing techniques to prevent air bubbles."},{"s":9,"e":1,"t":"The French Chef: The Artichoke","a":"1971-10-06","l":29},{"s":9,"e":2,"t":"Tarts Aux Fruites (Fruit Tarts)","a":"1971-10-13","l":29,"img":"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/71713/4206935.jpg"},{"s":9,"e":3,"t":"To Roast a Turkey","a":"1971-10-20","l":29},{"s":9,"e":4,"t":"French Croissants","a":"1971-10-27","l":29,"img":"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/71713/4206937.jpg"},{"s":9,"e":5,"t":"Soup Du Jour","a":"1971-11-03","l":28},{"s":9,"e":6,"t":"Terrines and Pâtés","a":"1971-11-10","l":28},{"s":9,"e":7,"t":"Madeleines and Génoise Jelly Roll","a":"1971-11-17","l":28},{"s":9,"e":8,"t":"To Make a Bûche","a":"1971-11-24","l":28},{"s":9,"e":9,"t":"The French Chef: Le Cocktail","a":"1971-12-01","l":28},{"s":9,"e":10,"t":"Gallic Pot Roast","a":"1971-12-08","l":28,"img":"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/71713/4206943.jpg"},{"s":9,"e":11,"t":"Cheese Souffle","a":"1971-12-15","l":28},{"s":9,"e":12,"t":"The Good Loaf","a":"1971-12-22","l":28},{"s":9,"e":13,"t":"The Hollandaise Family","a":"1971-12-29","l":28},{"s":9,"e":14,"t":"Cold Soufflés and Bavarian Cream","a":"1972-01-05","l":28},{"s":9,"e":15,"t":"Case for Salmon","a":"1972-01-12","l":28,"img":"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/71713/4206948.jpg"},{"s":9,"e":16,"t":"Orange Bavarian Cream","a":"1972-01-19","l":28,"img":"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/71713/4206949.jpg"},{"s":9,"e":17,"t":"To Stuff a Cabbage","a":"1972-01-26","l":28,"img":"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/71713/4206950.jpg"},{"s":9,"e":18,"t":"Tripes à la Mode","a":"1972-01-30","l":28,"img":"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/71713/4206951.jpg"},{"s":9,"e":19,"t":"Elegance with Aspic","a":"1972-02-06","l":28,"img":"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/71713/4206952.jpg"},{"s":9,"e":20,"t":"Orange Bavarian Cream","a":"1972-02-13","l":28,"d":"Julia Child demonstrates how to make Bavarian cream using egg whites, whipped cream, gelatin and bourbon whiskey. She flavors the cream with hazelnuts then molds it in a souffle dish with some bourbon soaked cake and the cream."},{"s":9,"e":21,"t":"Ham Transformation","a":"1972-02-20","l":28},{"s":9,"e":22,"t":"Ice Cream","a":"1972-02-27","l":28,"img":"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/71713/4206955.jpg"},{"s":10,"e":1,"t":"For Working Guys and Gals","a":"1972-10-01","l":28},{"s":10,"e":2,"t":"Small Kitchen, Big Ideas","a":"1972-10-08","l":28},{"s":10,"e":3,"t":"Coffee and Brioche","a":"1972-10-15","l":28},{"s":10,"e":4,"t":"Brunch for a Bunch","a":"1972-10-22","l":28},{"s":10,"e":5,"t":"VIP Cake","a":"1972-10-29","l":28,"img":"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/episodes/71713/4206964.jpg"},{"s":10,"e":6,"t":"The French Chef: Brunch For A Bunch","a":"1972-11-05","l":28},{"s":10,"e":7,"t":"Sudden Company","a":"1972-11-12","l":28},{"s":10,"e":8,"t":"First Course Sit Down Dinner","a":"1972-11-19","l":28},{"s":10,"e":9,"t":"Main Course Sit Down Dinner","a":"1972-11-26","l":28,"d":"Creating a main course featuring a beef tenderloin."},{"s":10,"e":10,"t":"Grand Finale Sit Down Dinner","a":"1972-12-03","l":28},{"s":10,"e":11,"t":"Kids Want to Cook","a":"1972-12-10","l":28},{"s":10,"e":12,"t":"The French Chef: Grand Finale Sit Down Dinner","a":"1972-12-17","l":28},{"s":10,"e":13,"t":"The French Chef: Kids Want To Cook","a":"1972-12-24","l":28,"d":"After you’ve mastered French puff pastry, try this recipe for Le Pithiviers, a glorious almond tart."}]}